Package: mssrscopR
Title: Single-Frame Mean-Shift Super-Resolution Structure Maps
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("R.", "Heller",
           email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Computes the single-frame Mean-Shift Super-Resolution ('MSSR')
    structure map of Torres-Garcia et al. (2022) <doi:10.1038/s41467-022-34693-9>
    with an independently written implementation that keeps the input
    orientation, accepts non-square frames and defines the result for flat
    input. Provides output-grid coordinates, structural masks for measuring
    the original data, pixel-wise temporal statistics of the per-frame maps
    of an image sequence (mean, variance and lagged SOFI cumulants as defined
    in the article's supplement), a self-test against bundled synthetic
    fixtures and an interactive 'shiny' app for exploring parameters.
    Results are structural maps, not quantitative intensities; no gain in
    physical resolution or benefit for any application is implied.
